B.t0=new A.bT(B.G2,["ASSESS PHYSIOLOGICAL STABILITY FOR ENTERAL FEEDING","UNSTABLE / CONTRAINDICATION PRESENT","STABLE / NO FEEDING CONTRAINDICATION","TOTAL DAILY FLUID REQUIREMENT","Maintenance IV fluid type","IV REVIEW \u2192 TRANSITION TO FEEDS","MILK SOURCE","ROUTE OF FEEDING","STANDARD START","CAUTIOUS START: AEDF/REDF","CAUTIOUS START: VERY SMALL INFANTS","FULL FEEDS","MONITORING","POOR WEIGHT GAIN","Iron","Vitamin D","Calcium / phosphorus",u.aW,"DOs","DON\u2019Ts","KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS (KPIs)","RELATED INFORMATION","ABBREVIATIONS","REFERENCES"],t.li)
B.afd=s(["LOOK FOR: Shock / poor perfusion \u2022 Recurrent apnoea requiring intervention / respiratory failure \u2022 Ongoing seizures with physiological instability \u2022 Severe hypothermia \u2022 Concerning abdominal signs: bilious vomiting, bloody stools, marked or progressive distension, tenderness or discoloration"],t.s)
B.a9G=s(["Stabilize and treat the cause","Start appropriate IV fluids","Reassess clinical stability and readiness to start enteral feeds"],t.s)
B.adm=s(["Start / continue enteral feeds at the earliest","Continue the tolerated feed volume in referred babies","Choose route by gestational maturity and clinical status"],t.s)
B.a4r=s(["ENTERAL + IV + OTHER FLUID INPUTS. Starting guide (mL/kg/day): Use day of life (D), not day of admission","BW <1000 g OR GA <28 wk: D1 80; D2 90; D3 100; D4 120; D5 140; D6 150; D7 150\u2013160","BW \u22651000 g AND GA \u226528 wk: D1 60; D2 80; D3 100; D4 120; D5 140; D6 150; D7 150\u2013160"],t.s)
B.a8I=s(["First 48 h: 10% dextrose","After 48 h: Review serum Na, urine output and weight change before adding sodium. N/5 in 10% dextrose is an option; adjust for IV volume and enteral intake","KCl: usually 2 mmol/kg/day; review urine output, serum K and other K intake first"],t.s)
B.a7_=s(["Adjust total fluids and electrolytes as per daily weight change, urine output, blood glucose and clinical status","IV volume = total fluids \u2212 feeds \u2212 other fluid inputs","Start feeds after stabilization; taper IV as feeds progress; maintain hydration / glucose"],t.s)
B.a8N=s(["Preferred milk, in order: Mother\u2019s own milk (MOM) \u2192 Pasteurized donor human milk \u2192 Appropriate formula if human milk unavailable","Start expression within 1 h of birth; repeat every 2\u20133 h","Use LMU for expression support, safe collection, storage and timely provision of MOM","Colostrum care: Apply mother\u2019s own colostrum to buccal mucosa every 2\u20134 h when oral feeding is not possible"],t.s)
B.a7D=s(["STANDARD START. APPLIES TO: GA \u226528 wk AND BW \u22651000 g, without antenatal AEDF/REDF; GA \u226535 wk, including antenatal AEDF/REDF\u2020. Start time*: As soon as possible after birth. Start volume: 60 mL/kg/day. Advance daily as tolerated: 20\u201330 mL/kg/day. If BW <1000 g, use the third column irrespective of gestation. *Start once clinically stable, with reassuring abdominal assessment. \u2020At \u226535 wk, AEDF/REDF alone does not require restricted feeds or IV fluids; individualize by clinical and abdominal assessment."],t.s)
B.a4T=s(["CAUTIOUS START: AEDF/REDF. APPLIES TO: GA 28\u201334\u2076 wk AND BW \u22651000 g, with antenatal AEDF/REDF. Start time*: As soon as stable; aim by 12 h. Start volume: 20 mL/kg/day. Advance daily as tolerated: 20\u201330 mL/kg/day. If BW <1000 g, use the third column irrespective of gestation. *Start once clinically stable, with reassuring abdominal assessment. \u2020At \u226535 wk, AEDF/REDF alone does not require restricted feeds or IV fluids; individualize by clinical and abdominal assessment."],t.s)
B.af0=s(["CAUTIOUS START: VERY SMALL INFANTS. APPLIES TO: GA <28 wk OR BW <1000 g. Start time*: As soon as stable; aim by 12 h. Start volume: 10\u201320 mL/kg/day. Advance daily as tolerated: 20 mL/kg/day. If BW <1000 g, use the third column irrespective of gestation. *Start once clinically stable, with reassuring abdominal assessment. \u2020At \u226535 wk, AEDF/REDF alone does not require restricted feeds or IV fluids; individualize by clinical and abdominal assessment."],t.s)
B.a8Q=s(["If BW <1000 g, use the third column irrespective of gestation.","*Start once clinically stable, with reassuring abdominal assessment.","\u2020At \u226535 wk, AEDF/REDF alone does not require restricted feeds or IV fluids; individualize by clinical and abdominal assessment.","FULL FEEDS: usually 150\u2013180 mL/kg/day; individualize to growth and clinical status","FREQUENCY: 2-hourly; consider 3-hourly when PMA >32 wk, stable, on full feeds and off respiratory support","VOLUME PER FEED: daily enteral volume (mL) \xf712 (2-hourly) or \xf78 (3-hourly)"],t.s)
B.acS=s(["Before each feed: Clinical condition, vomiting and visible abdominal distension; verify feeding-tube position when used","Daily: Weight change, actual milk intake and urine output; glucose / electrolytes as indicated","Weekly: Plot weight, length and head circumference on INTERGROWTH-21st postnatal growth charts","Immediately if warning signs: Abdominal signs: bilious vomiting, bloody stools, marked/progressive distension, tenderness/discoloration; Any systemic clinical deterioration","Do not routinely check pre-feed gastric residuals or abdominal girth in well babies without signs of feeding intolerance.","Measure girth serially when there is distension or clinical concern."],t.s)
B.a8O=s(["Assess: actual milk intake/transfer, thermal stress, illness, anaemia and possible sodium deficiency","Optimize: correct identified causes; consider 180\u2013200 mL/kg/day if tolerated and no fluid restriction","Review nutrient adequacy: Consider fortification if protein, energy or mineral intake remains insufficient"],t.s)
B.a7a=s(["Iron: Human-milk-fed preterm OR LBW infants. Elemental iron: BW <1500 g: 2\u20133 mg/kg/day; BW 1500\u20132499 g: 2 mg/kg/day. Start at 2 weeks of age once feeds are established. Continue to 6 months, then follow Anemia Mukt Bharat."],t.s)
B.a4I=s(["Vitamin D: Consider in human-milk-fed preterm/LBW infants. 400\u2013800 IU/day. As per unit protocol. Start once feeds are established; review at discharge and follow-up."],t.s)
B.a8f=s(["Calcium / phosphorus: Prioritize BW <1500 g OR GA <32 wk on unfortified human milk; others by intake / bone-disease risk. Preterm total intake targets: Ca 120\u2013200; P 70\u2013115 mg/kg/day. Supplement the shortfall. Monitor P / ALP in at-risk infants. Review at term PMA; continue if intake is inadequate or tests remain abnormal."],t.s)
B.a63=s([u.aW,"Consider Zinc in human-milk-fed preterm or LBW infants."],t.s)
B.a7r=s(["Prioritize mother\u2019s own milk; help mothers express and breastfeed","Start enteral feeds at the earliest; advance rapidly as per tolerance","Review actual intake, growth and total fluids daily"],t.s)
B.adX=s(["Do not delay feeds without a clinical contraindication","Do not routinely check gastric residuals or abdominal girth","Do not overlook bilious vomiting, bloody stools or abdominal signs"],t.s)
B.a8W=s(["Timely breastmilk feeding (%): Preterm/LBW neonates requiring facility-based care who received breastmilk within 12 h of birth (inborn) or admission (outborn) / All preterm/LBW neonates requiring facility-based care \xd7100. Target \u226580%","Exclusive breastmilk feeding at discharge (%): Preterm/LBW neonates admitted to SNCU/NICU who received exclusive breastmilk in the final 24 h before discharge / Eligible preterm/LBW neonates discharged alive from SNCU/NICU \xd7100. Target \u226590%"],t.s)
B.afu=s(["RELATED INFORMATION","Expressing the first milk","Cup / paladai feeding","Feeding low-birth-weight babies","NNF clinical practice guideline"],t.s)
B.aeX=s(["ABBREVIATIONS","AEDF: Absent end-diastolic flow","ALP: Alkaline phosphatase","BW: Birth weight","D: Day of life","GA: Gestational age","IV: Intravenous","KCl: Potassium chloride","LBW: Low birth weight","LMU: Lactation management unit","MOM: Mother\u2019s own milk","NICU: Neonatal intensive care unit","OG: Orogastric","PMA: Postmenstrual age","REDF: Reversed end-diastolic flow","SNCU: Special newborn care unit"],t.s)
B.ahe=new A.bT(B.G2,[B.afd,B.a9G,B.adm,B.a4r,B.a8I,B.a7_,B.a8N,B.A9,B.a7D,B.a4T,B.af0,B.a8Q,B.acS,B.a8O,B.a7a,B.a4I,B.a8f,B.a63,B.a7r,B.adX,B.a8W,B.afu,B.aeX,B.AK],t.VJ)
